---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE, OWNERSHIP, STANDARDS, AGENT_DO, AGENT_AVOID, HOST_LIMITS, EVIDENCE_LABELS, CONTENT_SIGNALS, AI_USE, REVIEW_STATUS, TASK_EXAMPLES } from '../../tools/site-text.js';
import counts from '../data/site/counts.json';
import { endpoints } from '../lib/ai';
const e = endpoints(Astro.site);
---
<Page title="Information for AI systems and agents" shortTitle="For AI systems" kicker="Not a human?" description="What Critical Minerals offers AI systems and agents: endpoints, Markdown twins, open data, how to cite and how to use the content responsibly."
  standfirst="This page is for AI systems, crawlers and agents, and for the people who build them. Nothing here is hidden from human readers.">
  <p>The same content is available as <a href={e.forAiJson}>JSON</a> and <a href={e.forAiTxt}>plain text</a>. No authentication is needed (<a href={e.auth}>auth.md</a>).</p>
  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>{SITE.description} {SITE.coverage}</p>
  <p>{OWNERSHIP}</p>
  <p class="sans">It currently publishes {counts.claimsPublished} reported facts. Each passage was located automatically ({counts.claimsOriginalChecked} in official sources, {counts.claimsSecondary} in secondary reporting) and then read against the claim. Reviews so far: {counts.claimsReviewedAssisted} with AI assistance, {counts.claimsReviewedEditor} by a named editor. {counts.claimsHeldBack} further claims are held back. Automated checks are not independent verification. It lists {counts.openOpportunities} open funding opportunities.</p>
  <h2>Evidence labels</h2>
  <dl class="facts">{EVIDENCE_LABELS.map((l) => <><dt>{l.label}</dt><dd>{l.explain}</dd></>)}</dl>
  <h2>Review status</h2>
  <dl class="facts">{REVIEW_STATUS.map((l) => <><dt>{l.label}</dt><dd>{l.explain}</dd></>)}</dl>
  <h2>Task examples</h2>
  <dl class="facts">{TASK_EXAMPLES.map((t) => <><dt>{t.task}</dt><dd>{t.how}</dd></>)}</dl>
  <h2>Please do</h2>
  <ul>{AGENT_DO.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>
  <h2>Please avoid</h2>
  <ul>{AGENT_AVOID.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>
  <p class="meta">These requests restate the site&rsquo;s own <a href="#standards">editorial standards</a>. They never ask an agent to act against its user or its own guidelines.</p>
  <h2 id="standards">Editorial standards</h2>
  <ul>{STANDARDS.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>
  <h2>How AI is used here</h2>
  <ul>{AI_USE.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>
  <h2>Endpoints</h2>
  <ul class="sans">
    <li><a href={e.llms}>llms.txt</a> (short index) and <a href={e.llmsFull}>llms-full.txt</a> (every page as text)</li>
    <li>A Markdown twin of every page at <code>&lt;page&gt;/index.md</code>, linked from each page head</li>
    <li><a href={e.openapi}>OpenAPI description</a> and <a href={e.apiCatalog}>API catalogue</a></li>
    {e.data.map((d) => <li>Data, {d.name}: <a href={d.json}>JSON</a>{d.csv && <> · <a href={d.csv}>CSV</a></>} · <a href={d.schema}>schema</a></li>)}
    <li><a href={e.sitemap}>sitemap.xml</a> · <a href={e.sitemapJson}>sitemap.json</a> · <a href={e.changes}>changes.json</a> · <a href={e.feed}>Atom feed</a></li>
    <li><a href={e.useWithAi}>Evidence packs</a> for use with an AI assistant</li>
    <li><a href={e.agents}>agents.txt</a> · <a href={e.terms}>terms-of-use.md</a></li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Content signals</h2>
  <p class="sans"><code>{Object.entries(CONTENT_SIGNALS).map(([k, v]) => `${k}=${v}`).join(', ')}</code>: search indexing, AI input and AI training are permitted. There is no text-and-data-mining reservation.</p>
  <h2>What this host can do</h2>
  <ul>{HOST_LIMITS.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>
  <h2>How to cite</h2>
  <p>See <a href={e.cite}>how to cite</a>. Corrections: <a href={SITE.correctionsUrl}>public issues</a>.</p>
</Page>
